# soul/axes -- the coordinate system. Owner-only, like everything in soul/.
#
# A path is a point flattened in one axis order. This file says which segment is which axis,
# so the same cells can be re-addressed in any other order.
#
#   PATTERN [axis=value ...]   a path family. First matching line wins.
#       literal                  must equal the segment
#       <axis>                   binds one segment
#       pre<axis>suf             binds a segment minus literal text around it
#       <axis...>                binds the rest of the path (last segment only)
#       axis=value               a constant coordinate for every cell in this family
#
#   view NAME AXIS...          a derived tree at refs/pp/NAME, addressed by these axes in this
#                              order. A cell is in the view if it has the first axis; axes it
#                              lacks are skipped. Every cell also has `path` and `hash`
#                              (written ab/cdef..., fanned out the way .git/objects is).
#                              Naming `seq` makes the view range over every appearance in
#                              history (seq = position on main + commit) instead of the tip.

inbox/<task>.fx/<effect...>            state=inbox    part=fx
inbox/<task>                           state=inbox    part=task
claimed/<body>/<task>.fx/<effect...>   state=claimed  part=fx
claimed/<body>/<task>                  state=claimed  part=task
done/<task>/fx/<effect...>             state=done     part=fx
done/<task>/<part...>                  state=done
bodies/<body>/<part...>                state=self
soul/<part...>

view by-task  task state body part effect
view by-body  body state task part effect
view by-hash  hash seq path
